First, we sketch the set ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}:$ \n\n![](images/f0/f02e2138f843c5a350c8be6c81a408c4af51fb9b19ced3fa26bfc466493008ac.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, to get the truth set of $P(x)∨Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{p}$ or ${T}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/45/45e38853893ceec19f969a1611cd50bbb9ff97e7bfd617c6e2e0a6268fb4b8fa.png)\n\nAs a result, we get the following diagram:\n\n![](images/dd/dde2aacce3d0707ddb09c06ca305645eadba1aedca9858eacc24abd46d09b03c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381644 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198259 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "264cfe66-691e-550e-97ad-b71924332f21" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Implication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ebb999a-dcd7-59c8-ae67-e4b0d1b4ebb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{5,15,25,35\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434431} {:answer/id #uuid "5826c839-6514-58d5-b7ad-37f4b9d17f20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{25\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434432} {:answer/id #uuid "91f26d38-d7ad-54b2-8893-934a3a454856" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{10,20,30\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434436} {:answer/id #uuid "c7e4d5ce-7267-5b6d-8a25-095f9eebaa99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{5,15,35\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434441} {:answer/id #uuid "d48c3def-d0f9-52d3-be15-de9c130118a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{10,20,25,30\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d48c3def-d0f9-52d3-be15-de9c130118a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{10,20,25,30\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434442} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec655a18-47df-5955-b97c-fd9b1dce4fb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "449791a5-eb97-5069-9e57-e5460d7f72bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-183317" :question/problem "For the universal set $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU=\\{5,10,15,20,25,30,35\\},\n$$\n\nfind the truth set of $P(x)⇒Q(x)$ for the following predicates: \n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is odd.\n\n- $Q(x):$ $\\sqrt{x}$ is integer." :question/worked-solution "Since $P(x)⇒Q(x)≡¬P(x)∨Q(x),$ the corresponding truth sets can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={T}_{¬P∨Q} \\\\  & ={T}_{¬P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{P}=\\{5,15,25,35\\}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the complement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\overset{―}{T}}_{P} & =\\overset{―}{\\{5,15,25,35\\}} \\\\  & =\\{10,20,30\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}=\\{25\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇒Q} & ={\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cup {T}_{Q} \\\\  & =\\{10,20,30\\}\\cup \\{25\\} \\\\  & =\\{10,20,25,30\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381672 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198261 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d6db336-845a-506a-b020-cced1b38e23a" :knowledge-point/title "Using Laws Involving Implications and Equivalences"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "209d2bd5-6761-5c94-ba92-88b5074ca51b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381674} {:answer/id #uuid "199c8724-565e-5dce-ad7e-bfa2f74b7250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381675} {:answer/id #uuid "e4cd27b5-8f1c-59bc-ba84-fd4c32304501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381676} {:answer/id #uuid "c2374090-35ce-576f-8a84-1f7140d89d0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381677} {:answer/id #uuid "7c6cbc35-ea42-58a4-bbec-262e4e83fef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c6cbc35-ea42-58a4-bbec-262e4e83fef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381678} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdc97073-4b1c-5916-9f40-170a84490dd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381673}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf3548ae-a137-5c57-8262-82ca0ade3b9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-183356" :question/problem "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$ \n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\nI. $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ is equivalent to  $x\\in N.$\n\nII. $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ if and only if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$\n\nIII. If $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ then $x\\in \\{3,7\\},$ or if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}$ then $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N.$" :question/worked-solution "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ if and only if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$\n\n- $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ is equivalent to $x\\in \\{3,7\\}.$\n\n- If $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N$ then $x\\in \\{3,7\\},$ and if $x\\in \\{3,7\\}$ then $x\\in \\{-1,0,3,7\\}\\cap N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c5f2a86-209a-5bb3-a3f2-77d679adb0a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10fd375b-d7d6-5467-8bdb-6f37bc432d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434429} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb4114b-80de-58c7-a9c6-c2e4caceaeef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434433} {:answer/id #uuid "9acebaf5-8307-528a-b69c-75e7d4aa4e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434437} {:answer/id #uuid "9b4b0d88-2d4c-57d0-b244-861d5aa82dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434438} {:answer/id #uuid "c57b9858-4955-5a75-af05-c5a6fbbab5b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-3,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b4b0d88-2d4c-57d0-b244-861d5aa82dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,3]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434438} :answer-field/id #uuid "74cac60f-4eb1-54cb-950d-4d03ca15d20c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28a2abe2-d607-5ca5-a1d6-25d691cd727c" :question/math-academy-id "q-183378" :question/problem "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n- $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}\\le 9$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $5x-3>7$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\le 9 \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is \n${T}_{P}=[-3,3].$ \nAs a result, the complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ).$\n\n- To find the truth set of $Q(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-3 & >7 \\\\ 5x & >10 \\\\ x & >2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $Q(x)$ is\n${T}_{Q}=(2,\\infty ),$\nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=(-\\infty ,2].$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =[-3,3]\\cap (2,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(2,3] \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =((-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (3,\\infty ))\\cap (-\\infty ,2] \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3) \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =(2,3]\\cup (-\\infty ,-3) \\\\  & =(-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (2,3].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407604 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198260 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c5f2a86-209a-5bb3-a3f2-77d679adb0a4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Truth Set of an Equivalence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02aa5a20-9201-5d23-8cf5-2deba4b15914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3e/3e44b650b220edc54c55a6407d3d8f221621fdd2109019cba04541239904eabf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407573} {:answer/id #uuid "08ce88cb-1fec-5ee5-a225-451721870f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a8/a8aca0881a2d233f604ccf65721fb3ee8f1e2a4a1f0f58d361aca510a28c6ccb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407575} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc43e02-7934-5003-87eb-e5f659b120a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f5/f54783549b17bd359af35f39fc72463e051f55669b5217c885e39af4610b4ef6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407586} {:answer/id #uuid "a6cb35c6-3424-599a-9911-49fc63bbf088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/07/070e2e754f2751e43fef94ccee1b9b6b3596e0f60f6328ee5b7cf693c2bc4460.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407590} {:answer/id #uuid "f1cef8d6-a596-58df-b04d-b02c0eda4b04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/52/52fa819daef857ea6f752b1b1b1d0e4921a5714627101513ac16a6a0bb83f78f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08ce88cb-1fec-5ee5-a225-451721870f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a8/a8aca0881a2d233f604ccf65721fb3ee8f1e2a4a1f0f58d361aca510a28c6ccb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407575} :answer-field/id #uuid "cde9ec8b-5f65-5e06-a601-75f9c0e5fcaf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9d3f9714-3d36-5297-84a8-bc71c9dc5efe" :question/math-academy-id "q-183806" :question/problem "![](images/0b/0bf4de97259ad9382c60f3195f33aec1f429926914eed222257c997fd3dc3e60.png)\n\nThe shaded regions above represent the truth sets of predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x),$ defined over the universal set ${R}^{2}.$ Which of the following is the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since we have that \n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we sketch the set ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/c3/c339e66441c947025f700d4206542e2a54bebf23b6973b835026170c8871eecf.png)\n\nThen, we sketch the set ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}$ and ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/5d/5d0ea62a7e98b8383e436586cefd2065667eadd54caaa3006950add1c335a9ce.png)\n\nAs a result, ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}$ is the following: \n\n![](images/05/05873c0302db6dc55a078962f99da6a6dc9fa1dbbdd75b688e0f503277d66f1c.png)\n\nFinally, to get the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x),$ we take all the points that belong to ${T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}$ or ${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}:$\n\n![](images/a8/a8aca0881a2d233f604ccf65721fb3ee8f1e2a4a1f0f58d361aca510a28c6ccb.png)"}]}
